  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Neopets co-creator Adam Powell began programming on a ZX Spectrum at five and wrote his own adventure books at school. His first computer text adventure recreated his university accommodation, complete with hostile cleaners and rubbish heaps. The programme exhausted its memory before players could leave the building. Work on a multiplayer university game subsequently helped him develop Neopets.\n\nAt Meteor Games, Powell wanted players to enjoy an online world in short sessions. His proposed payment model combined subscriptions with purchases of decorative houses, clothes and pets. He opposed selling competitive advantages: extra spending would change a player's appearance, without buying greater powers.",
